 of escaping their  mining town her character was an  advocate and a source of strength for  the boys throughout and served as one of  the only likable adults in the movie  recount in 2008 Dern helped HBO rehash a  political scandal in the TV movie  recount which followed the controversy  surrounding the 2000 presidential  election in the film Dern plays  Katherine Harris then secretary of state  of Florida where a recount controversy  erupted between  candidates George W Bush and Al Gore  jernt earned her second Golden Globe win  for the part and was also nominated for  an Emmy a SAG Award and more Dern said  she learned a great deal from the  experience of playing such a  controversial real-life figure telling  the Washington Post recount taught me a  lot because my dad told me you can never  hate the characters you play and you  have to love your characters I had to  just figure out how to give some  humanity and depth of passion to a  person that had become a huge stereotype  in this country enlightened her next  small screen role of note was in HBO's  critically acclaimed dramedy series  enlightened on the show Dern played Amy  Jellicoe a woman who after a nervous  breakdown comes back to work with a new  outlook on life  Dern collected another Golden Globe win  and an Emmy nomination for the show and  served as both co-creator and star  however like many critically acclaimed  dramas in the era of peak TV and lighten  never found a big audience and the show  was canceled after just two seasons The  Fault in Our Stars in 2014  turn went back to the mainstream for the  teen oriented romantic comedy The Fault  in Our Stars the movie based on the John  Green novel of the same name featured  Dern as the mother of shailene Woodley's  hazel grace Lancaster a teenager who  falls in love while she deals with  terminal thyroid cancer the film is a  critical success and arrived as a  box-office smash wild it took turn over  20 years to earn another Academy Award  nomination after ramblin rose but her  not for 2014's Wilde was certainly well  deserved Dern starred in the film as the  mother of Reese Witherspoon Cheryl  Strayed who flashes back to her  childhood as she hikes up the Pacific  Crest Trail trying to discover her true  self not only was her performance  celebrated but it wouldn't be the last  buzzy collaboration she'd have with  Witherspoon big little lies HBO's latest  awards season darling big little lies  has earned nods for all of its main  stars at the Emmys the Golden Globes and  more in the series Dern plays Renata  Klein the uptight nemesis of Reese  Witherspoon's madeline mckenzie and Dern  walked away with a Golden Globe  nomination and an Emmy win beating out  her co-star shailene woodley for the  latter award although big little lies  was initially billed as a limited series  it's been renewed for a second season  following overwhelming fandom  thanks for watching click the looper  icon to subscribe to our YouTube channel  let's check out all this cool stuff we  know you'll love to  [Music]
 

